From 0b000b8e4db4ea69abac6d5a27075764c2dc80c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 21:15:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Make it impossible to save a log under a date whose
 period hasn't happened
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sunday 12 Jul 2026 vanished from Insight because its log — uploaded at
02:07 Mon morning — was filed under report_date 2026-07-13. When the real
Monday log arrived the next night it collided with that row (UNIQUE
report_date), overwrote the header, and appended its incidents, leaving
Sunday empty and Monday holding both days. Same signature previously on
22-23 Jun 2026. The 8 Jul hardening only *warned* about a today-dated
log; at 2am the warning was ignored.

Three hard gates now run at the save boundary (upsertReportData), where
they protect every path regardless of UI behaviour:

1. Impossible period (never overridable): a log dated D covers D 06:00 →
   D+1 06:00 Europe/London; if that period hasn't started at save time
   the date cannot be right. This alone blocks all three historical
   incidents while allowing every legitimate upload in the DB's history
   (overnight uploads of yesterday's log, late backfills).
2. Row-vote mismatch: each incident's CCIL header line carries a
   machine-stamped DD/MM/YYYY HH:MM which the parser now retains
   (Incident.headerIsoDate). Freshly-started incidents must fall inside
   the log's own period, so a ≥60% majority of non-continuation rows
   pointing at a different 06:00→06:00 period blocks the save.
3. Collision guard: a re-upload whose CCIL refs overlap <25% with what
   the target date already stores is a different day's log, not a
   regeneration — blocked instead of silently interleaving two days.

Gates 2-3 are heuristic and can be consciously overridden via a button
that appears with the error; gate 1 cannot. The Roster step now blocks
"Continue to Review" (red banner + one-click correct-date button) for
the same two decisive conditions, so operators are stopped at the form,
not at the end of the flow. Blank logs started before 06:00 now default
to the period in progress (yesterday) instead of today.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
